        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>If we wish to sum the first <span class=\"math\">[MATH: N]</span> integers, an easy way is to use the following formula:\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: \u2211_(n = 1)^(N)n|= 1 + 2 + 3 + \u22ef + (N \u2212 1) + N; = (1)/(2)N(N + 1)]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "If we wish to sum the first [MATH: N] integers, an easy way is to use the following formula:\n[MATH: \u2211_(n = 1)^(N)n|= 1 + 2 + 3 + \u22ef + (N \u2212 1) + N; = (1)/(2)N(N + 1)]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>As we will see, we can use this simple formula to evaluate any series of the form <span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\displaystyle{\\sum_{n=1}^N (an+b)}.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "As we will see, we can use this simple formula to evaluate any series of the form [MATH: \\displaystyle{\\sum_{n=1}^N (an+b)}.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Content:\nIf we wish to sum the first [MATH: N] integers, an easy way is to use the following formula:\n[MATH: \u2211_(n = 1)^(N)n|= 1 + 2 + 3 + \u22ef + (N \u2212 1) + N; = (1)/(2)N(N + 1)]\n\nContent:\nAs we will see, we can use this simple formula to evaluate any series of the form [MATH: \\displaystyle{\\sum_{n=1}^N (an+b)}.]"
