        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "example_question",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Calculate <span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\displaystyle\\sum_{n=1}^{100} 4n.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "Calculate [MATH: \\displaystyle\\sum_{n=1}^{100} 4n.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>EXPLANATION</p>",
            "readable_text": "EXPLANATION",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>First, we take the factor <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 4]</span> outside the summation:\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\sum_{n=1}^{100} 4n = 4\\sum_{n=1}^{100} n]</span></p><p>Now, using the formula \n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: \u2211_(n = 1)^(N)n|= (1)/(2)N(N + 1)]</span>\nwith <span class=\"math\">[MATH: N=100,]</span> we get</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: 4\u2211_(n = 1)^(100)n|= 4((1)/(2) \u22c5 100 \u22c5 101); = 4 \u22c5 5050; = 20200.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "First, we take the factor [MATH: 4] outside the summation:\n[MATH: \\sum_{n=1}^{100} 4n = 4\\sum_{n=1}^{100} n]\n\nNow, using the formula\n[MATH: \u2211_(n = 1)^(N)n|= (1)/(2)N(N + 1)]\nwith [MATH: N=100,] we get\n\n[MATH: 4\u2211_(n = 1)^(100)n|= 4((1)/(2) \u22c5 100 \u22c5 101); = 4 \u22c5 5050; = 20200.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
