            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>We can write the summation as follows:\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: \u2211_(n = 1)^(200)(3n + 2)|= \u2211_(n = 1)^(200)3n + \u2211_(n = 1)^(200)2; = 3\u2211_(n = 1)^(200)n + 2\u2211_(n = 1)^(200)1]</span></p><p>Let&#x27;s consider the two series separately. </p><ul><li><p>For the first series, we use the formula\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\displaystyle \\sum_{n=1}^N n = \\dfrac 1 2 N (N+1)]</span>\nwith <span class=\"math\">[MATH: N=200,]</span> and we get\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: 3\u2211_(n = 1)^(200)n|= 3((1)/(2) \u22c5 200 \u22c5 201); = 3 \u22c5 20100; = 60300.]</span></p></li><li><p>In the second series, <span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\displaystyle{\\sum_{n=1}^{200} 1}]</span> is just <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 1]</span> added together <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 200]</span> times, which is <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 200 \\cdot 1 = 200.]</span> So, we have\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: 2\\sum_{n=1}^{200} 1 =2 \\cdot 200 = 400.]</span></p></li></ul><p>Finally, we have</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\sum_{n=1}^{200} (3n+2) = 60\\,300 + 400 = 60\\,700.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "We can write the summation as follows:\n[MATH: \u2211_(n = 1)^(200)(3n + 2)|= \u2211_(n = 1)^(200)3n + \u2211_(n = 1)^(200)2; = 3\u2211_(n = 1)^(200)n + 2\u2211_(n = 1)^(200)1]\n\nLet's consider the two series separately.\n\n- For the first series, we use the formula\n[MATH: \\displaystyle \\sum_{n=1}^N n = \\dfrac 1 2 N (N+1)]\nwith [MATH: N=200,] and we get\n[MATH: 3\u2211_(n = 1)^(200)n|= 3((1)/(2) \u22c5 200 \u22c5 201); = 3 \u22c5 20100; = 60300.]\n- In the second series, [MATH: \\displaystyle{\\sum_{n=1}^{200} 1}] is just [MATH: 1] added together [MATH: 200] times, which is [MATH: 200 \\cdot 1 = 200.] So, we have\n[MATH: 2\\sum_{n=1}^{200} 1 =2 \\cdot 200 = 400.]\n\nFinally, we have\n\n[MATH: \\sum_{n=1}^{200} (3n+2) = 60\\,300 + 400 = 60\\,700.]",
            "images": [],
